# Flutter & Dart Architect - Cursor AI Rules (.cursorrules)
# Architecture: Clean Architecture by Feature + Decoupled Dio + Extension Types + Result/Either

You are an expert Flutter & Dart Software Architect. Always adhere to the following strict architectural rules:

## 1. Directory & Layer Organization
- Organize code by Feature under `lib/features/{feature}/`:
  - `data/`: `datasources/`, `models/`, `repositories/`
  - `domain/`: `entities/`, `repositories/` (interfaces), `usecases/`
  - `presentation/`: `pages/`, `controllers/`, `widgets/`
  - `{feature}_routes.dart`
  - `{feature}_dependencies.dart`
- Core cross-cutting modules live in `lib/core/` (`network/`, `error/`, `di/`, `navigation/`, `theme/`, `utils/`).
- Shared UI components live in `lib/shared/`.

## 2. Layer Constraints & Boundaries
- DOMAIN LAYER:
  - NEVER import `package:flutter/...` or `package:dio/...` or anything from `data/`.
  - Entities are pure immutable Dart classes with NO `fromJson` / `toJson`.
  - Repository contracts are abstract interfaces (`abstract interface class IFeatureRepository`).
  - UseCases have a single responsibility (`call(...)`) and return `Future<Either<Failure, T>>`.
- DATA LAYER:
  - Models MUST be Dart 3.3+ Extension Types: `extension type FeatureModel(FeatureEntity entity) implements FeatureEntity`.
  - Encapsulate `fromJson` and `toJson` strictly inside the Extension Type model.
  - DataSources MUST be CONCRETE classes (no abstract interfaces). They receive `IHttpClient`, accept raw primitive parameters/maps, return `HttpResponse<dynamic>`, and NEVER contain `try/catch` or business logic.
  - Repositories (`implements IFeatureRepository`) catch `HttpNetworkException`, map to `Failure`, deserialize `response.data` using `Model.fromJson(...)`, and return `Either<Failure, Entity>`.
- PRESENTATION LAYER:
  - NEVER call DataSources or concrete Repositories directly.
  - Inject controllers via `locator.get<Controller>()` or execute UseCases.
  - Represent state as a `sealed class {Feature}State`.
  - UI consumes state using exhaustive pattern-matching `switch (state)` with NO default branch.
  - Build UI using small, focused, private `StatelessWidget` classes. Avoid giant build methods.
  - Use `const` constructors wherever possible.

## 3. Network & Authentication
- NEVER import `package:dio` inside `features/`. Use `IHttpClient` interface.
- 401 Refresh Token requests MUST use an isolated `cleanDio` instance (without interceptors) and a `Completer<bool>` concurrency lock to prevent infinite 401 refresh loops.

## 4. Error Handling
- Use lightweight `Either<Failure, Success>` for functional error handling.
- Do NOT import `dartz` or `fpdart`. Use the custom sealed class implementation in `core/error/either.dart`.
- Catch `HttpNetworkException` in repositories; never let low-level network errors bubble to the UI.

## 5. Navigation & Global Helpers
- Centralize named routes in `AppPages`.
- Combine feature routes in `CustomRouter.generateRoute`.
- Use `locator.get<NavigationController>()` for contextless navigation.
- Use `locator.get<CustomSnack>()` for global snackbars.
